{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (38.67%) to bacterial Amylocyclicin GRAVY: 0.563; Mol formula: C319H532N83O90S3; Mol Wt: 7089.397, and Mol ex coeff.: 16650. Production and purification: This peptide was produced during the exponential phase. Purified from the overnight supernatant in 2 steps. Activity: Inhibited the growth of B. cereus ATCC 14579 on solid medium. MIC: B. cereus ATCC 14579 and 49064 (MIC 0.29-0.39 uM) and L. monocytogenes strains LM201, CMC54002, ATCC 19115 (MIC 0.39-0.78 uM), B. amyloliquefaciens X1 (MIC6.25 uM), B. thuringiensis BMB171 or YBT-1518 (MIC 0.39-0.78 uM), B. firmus DS-1 (MIC 3.13 uM), B. subtilis 168 (MIC 1.56 uM), B. pumilus SCG1 (MIC 12.5 uM), and E. faecalis ATCC29212/ATCC51299 (MIC 6.25-12.5 uM). Not active against S.aureus ATCC29213/CMCC26003, E.coli BL21/DH5alpha, S.enterica serotype Paratyphi CMCC50094, P.aeruginosa ATCC27853, P.putida Pri3,. Cerecyclin is also able to inhibit spore outgrowth at greater than 0.125 uM. In vitro Toxicity: Not hemo.lytic till 500 uM (<2% hemolysis). The excellent activity and poor hemo.lytic toxicity of this candidate deserve further studies (potential lead). Antimicrobial robustness: It is more stable than nisin A in the range pH 7-10 and at 37oC and 65oC. Updated 7/2021", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "32487738", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "mSystems. 2020 Jun 2;5(3):e00047-20. doi: 10.1128/mSystems.00047-20. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03198", "source_id": "AP03198", "source_numeric_id": "03198", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03198", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "In Silico Analysis Highlights the Diversity and Novelty of Circular Bacteriocins in Sequenced Microbial Genomes", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
